<report>
<title>Spearman's rank correlation</title>

<p><in>sample_1</in> vs. <in>sample_2</in><br />
Observations per sample = <in>obs</in><br />
Spearman's score = <inu>ix</inu></p>

<p>Spearman's rank correlation coefficient (Rho) =  <inu>rho</inu></p>

<block name="noci"><p><warn>CI not calculated when rho is 1 or -1.</warn></p></block>
<block name="ci"><p><ci><in>pc</in>% CI for rho (Fisher's Z transformed) = <inu>from</inu> to <inu>to</inu></ci></p></block>
<block name="lown">

<p><warn>Can not consider probability with very small samples (n &lt; 4)</warn></p></block>
<block name="results">
<block name="nop"><p><warn>P not calculable</warn></p></block>
<block name="results">

<p><pval>Upper side <inp>p_u</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: positive correlation)<br />
<pval>Lower side <inp>p_l</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: negative correlation)<br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: any correlation)</p>
</block>
</block>
<block name="ties">

<p><pval>Ties present: exact P not used</pval></p>
</block>
</report>
